{"id":"c13504d25a0786f0","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-df-automorphic-representation.md","title":"Automorphic Representation","display":"df-automorphic-representation — Automorphic Representation","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-automorphic-representation","aliases":["58-df-automorphic-representation","Automorphic Representation"],"display":"df-automorphic-representation — Automorphic Representation","depends_on":["[[58-df-reductive-group]]","[[58-df-group]]","[[58-df-hilbert-space]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-automorphic-representation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-automorphic-representation</span><span>Automorphic Representation</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-automorphic-representation — Automorphic Representation"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"8790321df936a708\" href=\"?note=8790321df936a708\" title=\"58-df-reductive-group\">58-df-reductive-group</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ed71f39f59370734\" href=\"?note=ed71f39f59370734\" title=\"58-df-group\">58-df-group</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"58-df-hilbert-space\">58-df-hilbert-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G,m,i,e,R\\in V\">\\(G,m,i,e,R\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S(G,m,i,e,R,\\mathbb Q)\">\\(\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S(G,m,i,e,R,\\mathbb Q)\\)</span> (supplied reductive-group data, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"8790321df936a708\" href=\"?note=8790321df936a708\" title=\"58-df-reductive-group\">58-df-reductive-group</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal H=L^2(G(\\mathbb Q)\\backslash G(\\mathbb A))\">\\(\\mathcal H=L^2(G(\\mathbb Q)\\backslash G(\\mathbb A))\\)</span> with inner product <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B_{\\mathcal H}\">\\(B_{\\mathcal H}\\)</span> (automorphic Hilbert space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R^{\\mathrm{reg}}:G(\\mathbb A)\\to U(\\mathcal H,B_{\\mathcal H})\">\\(R^{\\mathrm{reg}}:G(\\mathbb A)\\to U(\\mathcal H,B_{\\mathcal H})\\)</span> (right-regular unitary action)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal H_\\pi,B_\\pi\">\\(\\mathcal H_\\pi,B_\\pi\\)</span> (nonzero closed invariant Hilbert subspace and inherited inner product)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi:G(\\mathbb A)\\to U(\\mathcal H_\\pi)\">\\(\\pi:G(\\mathbb A)\\to U(\\mathcal H_\\pi)\\)</span> (unitary group representation)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\\)</span> (Hilbert-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"58-df-hilbert-space\">58-df-hilbert-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AutomorphicRepresentationData}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{AutomorphicRepresentationData}_S\\)</span> (automorphic-subrepresentation predicate relative to the supplied reductive data)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}automorphic\\text{-}representation\\text{-}data} \\vdash \\mathrm{AutomorphicRepresentationData}_S(\\pi,G,m,i,e,R,\\mathcal H,B_{\\mathcal H},\\mathcal H_\\pi,B_\\pi,R^{\\mathrm{reg}})\\leftrightarrow\\left[\\begin{aligned}&amp;\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S(G,m,i,e,R,\\mathbb Q)\\land\\mathcal H=L^2(G(\\mathbb Q)\\backslash G(\\mathbb A))\\\\&amp;\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(\\mathcal H,B_{\\mathcal H})\\land\\mathcal H_\\pi\\subseteq\\mathcal H\\land\\mathcal H_\\pi\\neq\\{0\\}\\land\\overline{\\mathcal H_\\pi}=\\mathcal H_\\pi\\\\&amp;\\land B_\\pi=B_{\\mathcal H}\\upharpoonright(\\mathcal H_\\pi\\times\\mathcal H_\\pi)\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(\\mathcal H_\\pi,B_\\pi)\\\\&amp;\\land R^{\\mathrm{reg}}:G(\\mathbb A)\\to U(\\mathcal H,B_{\\mathcal H})\\land\\forall g,h\\in G(\\mathbb A)\\;\\bigl(R^{\\mathrm{reg}}(gh)=R^{\\mathrm{reg}}(g)\\circ R^{\\mathrm{reg}}(h)\\bigr)\\\\&amp;\\land\\pi:G(\\mathbb A)\\to U(\\mathcal H_\\pi,B_\\pi)\\land\\forall g,h\\in G(\\mathbb A)\\;(\\pi(gh)=\\pi(g)\\circ\\pi(h))\\\\&amp;\\land\\forall g\\in G(\\mathbb A)\\;\\bigl(\\pi(g)=R^{\\mathrm{reg}}(g)\\upharpoonright\\mathcal H_\\pi\\bigr)\\\\&amp;\\land\\forall W\\subseteq\\mathcal H_\\pi\\;\\Bigl(0\\in W\\land\\forall u,v\\in W\\;\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb C\\;(au+bv\\in W)\\land\\overline W=W\\\\&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall g\\in G(\\mathbb A)\\;(\\pi(g)[W]\\subseteq W)\\to W=\\{0\\}\\lor W=\\mathcal H_\\pi\\Bigr)\\end{aligned}\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}automorphic\\text{-}representation\\text{-}data} \\vdash \\mathrm{AutomorphicRepresentationData}_S(\\pi,G,m,i,e,R,\\mathcal H,B_{\\mathcal H},\\mathcal H_\\pi,B_\\pi,R^{\\mathrm{reg}})\\leftrightarrow\\left[\\begin{aligned}&amp;\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S(G,m,i,e,R,\\mathbb Q)\\land\\mathcal H=L^2(G(\\mathbb Q)\\backslash G(\\mathbb A))\\\\&amp;\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(\\mathcal H,B_{\\mathcal H})\\land\\mathcal H_\\pi\\subseteq\\mathcal H\\land\\mathcal H_\\pi\\neq\\{0\\}\\land\\overline{\\mathcal H_\\pi}=\\mathcal H_\\pi\\\\&amp;\\land B_\\pi=B_{\\mathcal H}\\upharpoonright(\\mathcal H_\\pi\\times\\mathcal H_\\pi)\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(\\mathcal H_\\pi,B_\\pi)\\\\&amp;\\land R^{\\mathrm{reg}}:G(\\mathbb A)\\to U(\\mathcal H,B_{\\mathcal H})\\land\\forall g,h\\in G(\\mathbb A)\\;\\bigl(R^{\\mathrm{reg}}(gh)=R^{\\mathrm{reg}}(g)\\circ R^{\\mathrm{reg}}(h)\\bigr)\\\\&amp;\\land\\pi:G(\\mathbb A)\\to U(\\mathcal H_\\pi,B_\\pi)\\land\\forall g,h\\in G(\\mathbb A)\\;(\\pi(gh)=\\pi(g)\\circ\\pi(h))\\\\&amp;\\land\\forall g\\in G(\\mathbb A)\\;\\bigl(\\pi(g)=R^{\\mathrm{reg}}(g)\\upharpoonright\\mathcal H_\\pi\\bigr)\\\\&amp;\\land\\forall W\\subseteq\\mathcal H_\\pi\\;\\Bigl(0\\in W\\land\\forall u,v\\in W\\;\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb C\\;(au+bv\\in W)\\land\\overline W=W\\\\&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall g\\in G(\\mathbb A)\\;(\\pi(g)[W]\\subseteq W)\\to W=\\{0\\}\\lor W=\\mathcal H_\\pi\\Bigr)\\end{aligned}\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This adopts the discrete automorphic-spectrum convention: the represented object is an irreducible closed unitary subrepresentation of the right-regular action.</li>\n<li>The upstream reductive-group atom certifies only supplied trivial-radical data, not that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R\">\\(R\\)</span> is the canonical unipotent radical. The predicate is therefore honestly data-relative rather than a context-free canonical reductivity claim.</li>\n<li>The quantified invariant objects are required to be closed complex linear subspaces; arbitrary closed invariant subsets do not express irreducibility.</li>\n<li>Local components: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi = \\otimes \\pi_v\">\\(\\pi = \\otimes \\pi_v\\)</span>; decomposes as restricted tensor product</li>\n<li>Function: automorphic form is vector in space of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi\">\\(\\pi\\)</span>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K\">\\(K\\)</span>-finite vectors</li>\n<li>Restricted tensor products and conjectural Langlands correspondences are downstream structure, not clauses of this definition.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Bump, Automorphic Forms and Representations</li>\n<li>Gelbart, An Elementary Introduction to the Langlands Program</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-reductive-group","status":"resolved","id":"8790321df936a708","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-reductive-group]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-group","status":"resolved","id":"ed71f39f59370734","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-group]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-hilbert-space","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-hilbert-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-reductive-group","status":"resolved","id":"8790321df936a708","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$G,m,i,e,R\\in V$ and $\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S(G,m,i,e,R,\\mathbb Q)$ (supplied reductive-group data, see [[58-df-reductive-group]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-hilbert-space","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S$ (Hilbert-space predicate, see [[58-df-hilbert-space]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"G,m,i,e,R\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S(G,m,i,e,R,\\mathbb Q)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal H=L^2(G(\\mathbb Q)\\backslash G(\\mathbb A))","display":false},{"tex":"B_{\\mathcal H}","display":false},{"tex":"R^{\\mathrm{reg}}:G(\\mathbb A)\\to U(\\mathcal H,B_{\\mathcal H})","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal H_\\pi,B_\\pi","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi:G(\\mathbb A)\\to U(\\mathcal H_\\pi)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{AutomorphicRepresentationData}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}automorphic\\text{-}representation\\text{-}data} \\vdash \\mathrm{AutomorphicRepresentationData}_S(\\pi,G,m,i,e,R,\\mathcal H,B_{\\mathcal H},\\mathcal H_\\pi,B_\\pi,R^{\\mathrm{reg}})\\leftrightarrow\\left[\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S(G,m,i,e,R,\\mathbb Q)\\land\\mathcal H=L^2(G(\\mathbb Q)\\backslash G(\\mathbb A))\\\\&\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(\\mathcal H,B_{\\mathcal H})\\land\\mathcal H_\\pi\\subseteq\\mathcal H\\land\\mathcal H_\\pi\\neq\\{0\\}\\land\\overline{\\mathcal H_\\pi}=\\mathcal H_\\pi\\\\&\\land B_\\pi=B_{\\mathcal H}\\upharpoonright(\\mathcal H_\\pi\\times\\mathcal H_\\pi)\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(\\mathcal H_\\pi,B_\\pi)\\\\&\\land R^{\\mathrm{reg}}:G(\\mathbb A)\\to U(\\mathcal H,B_{\\mathcal H})\\land\\forall g,h\\in G(\\mathbb A)\\;\\bigl(R^{\\mathrm{reg}}(gh)=R^{\\mathrm{reg}}(g)\\circ R^{\\mathrm{reg}}(h)\\bigr)\\\\&\\land\\pi:G(\\mathbb A)\\to U(\\mathcal H_\\pi,B_\\pi)\\land\\forall g,h\\in G(\\mathbb A)\\;(\\pi(gh)=\\pi(g)\\circ\\pi(h))\\\\&\\land\\forall g\\in G(\\mathbb A)\\;\\bigl(\\pi(g)=R^{\\mathrm{reg}}(g)\\upharpoonright\\mathcal H_\\pi\\bigr)\\\\&\\land\\forall W\\subseteq\\mathcal H_\\pi\\;\\Bigl(0\\in W\\land\\forall u,v\\in W\\;\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb C\\;(au+bv\\in W)\\land\\overline W=W\\\\&\\qquad\\land\\forall g\\in G(\\mathbb A)\\;(\\pi(g)[W]\\subseteq W)\\to W=\\{0\\}\\lor W=\\mathcal H_\\pi\\Bigr)\\end{aligned}\\right]","display":true},{"tex":"R","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi = \\otimes \\pi_v","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi","display":false},{"tex":"K","display":false}],"bytes":3511,"backlinks":[{"id":"560c33a2a83aebf2","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{AutomorphicRepresentationData}_S:V^{11}\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (see [[../batch12/58-df-automorphic-representation.md]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-156","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-automorphic-representation.md|58-df-automorphic-representation]]（batch12）"}],"outgoing":["8790321df936a708","ed71f39f59370734","b70ce791d5b1a19b","36d7463d215be751"]}